<p>The Rev. Jesse Jackson, a longtime US civil rights leader and two-time Democratic presidential contender, has died at 84. Tributes have come in from politicians and communities in the United States and abroad. Many accounts revisited his decades of activism and how he pushed issues such as voting rights, jobs, education, and health care into the national conversation. Some international coverage also underscored Jackson’s work beyond the US, including repeated trips to South Africa and other African nations. There, he was widely respected for opposing apartheid and for serving at times as a peace broker and a prominent representative of Black America.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/hpkiEIYdcOQKkL6Ps8C2QCk9QP0aioreZCOqqUrQCg0bo0xjw96cSRBUTnN_mugF1mQQG2dUve9DBIWaNyYMrWKKx-hysnzRhXXSkCg-iA5dHySVryj76Fc6d0Qisj2Ogh22tD_eVMozvYonHmZeTKkJtDscf8_HRzh7G1xIj8qWgMKxEIGmPD8L9AsKnZn16QmRg_rWWzjdBy3RU5k' alt='Jesse Jackson with Nelson Mandela in Johannesburg in 2005.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Notable US political tributes: Coverage highlighted condolences and statements from figures including Barack Obama, Joe Biden, Kamala Harris, and Donald Trump after Jackson’s death.</li><li>From protester to presidential contender: The Christian Science Monitor followed Jackson’s arc from early civil rights organizing to his two Democratic presidential runs, highlighting his long focus on expanding Black voting power.</li><li>Political legacy: Commentary argued that Jackson helped build a more diverse, coalition-driven style of Democratic politics—an approach that still shapes the party’s base and priorities.</li><li>Language and oratory: The Globe and Mail pointed to Jackson’s gift for message-making, saying his phrases and framing helped explain—and reshape—American public life for decades.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>African Union Commission chairperson Mahmoud Ali Youssouf: He praised Jackson as a leading figure whose life’s work resonated with Africa’s struggles for justice, dignity, equality and liberation. (<a href='https://allafrica.com/stories/202602180051.html'>allAfrica (African Union)</a>)</li><li>Arab American advocates (as reported by Al Jazeera): Advocates eulogised Jackson as a civil rights leader who welcomed their communities, used his platform to defend Palestine, and pushed for broader political inclusion. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/2/18/jesse-jackson-helped-empower-us-arabs-and-raise-palestinian-cause'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li><li>Chicago residents (as reported by BBC): Mourners said they feel lasting gratitude for Jackson’s local activism and the opportunities they connect to his work in the city. (<a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cn8z9qq25jno'>BBC News</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/02/17/world/africa/jesse-jackson-south-africa-apartheid.html'>In Africa, Jesse Jackson Was Esteemed for His Fight Against Apartheid</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/2/18/jesse-jackson-helped-empower-us-arabs-and-raise-palestinian-cause'>How Jesse Jackson helped empower US Arabs and lift up the Palestinian cause</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cn8z9qq25jno'>&#x27;We&#x27;re going to always be grateful&#x27; - Chicagoans mourn loss of Jesse Jackson</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://theweek.com/politics/instant-opinion-jesse-jackson-russia-ukraine-olympics'>‘The forces he united still shape the Democratic Party’</a> - theweek.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/reaction-to-death-of-us-civil-rights-leader-jesse-jackson'>Reactions to death of US civil rights leader Jesse Jackson</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.csmonitor.com/USA/Politics/2026/0217/jesse-jackson-appreciation'>Jesse Jackson’s journey from a South Carolina protest to presidential runs</a> - csmonitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/video-u